<title>UK: IBCA assigns AAA l-term to DSL Bank issue.</title>
<headline>IBCA assigns AAA l-term to DSL Bank issue.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>IBCA, the European credit rating agency, has assigned a long-term rating of AAA to the Deutsche Siedlungs- und Landesrentenbank (DSL Bank) LUF2 billion step-up coupon bonds 2007 issue.</p>
<p>&quot;The rating is based on the implied federal German guarantee for the obligations of DSL Bank,&quot; IBCA said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Lisa Wilson, international Bonds Unit +44 171 542 6137</p>
</text>
